    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="0977" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1485</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Mayer </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 167
                    of the 7th ultimo in which you enclose a copy of a memorandum handed to you by
                    Rear Admiral Knapp upon the subject of the relations between treaty officials of
                    the Haitian Government.</p>
                <p>The Department approves Admiral Knapp’s memorandum and concurs in the views which
                    he has expressed therein.</p>
                <p>Copies of your despatch and its enclosure have been forwarded to the Secretary of
                    the Navy with this Department’s comment thereon as above.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
